{"nodes":[{"id":"UFM-001","title":"Introduction to Advanced Semiconductor Manufacturing","description":"This node introduces the advanced semiconductor manufacturing industry, defining its critical role as the foundation of modern electronics. Students will learn about the core product, Integrated Circuits (ICs), understanding how billions of transistors are integrated onto a single wafer to power devices like smartphones and computers. We will cover the industry's immense significance in technological advancement and its impact on the global economy.","status":"locked"},{"id":"UFM-002","title":"Defining Characteristics of Advanced Wafer Fabs","description":"Explore the 'four high' characteristics that define advanced wafer manufacturing: high technology, high precision, high cleanliness, and high automation. This node will detail how nano-scale manufacturing, AI-driven automation, quantum physics principles, and ultra-clean environments are critical for producing high-quality integrated circuits. Students will understand the stringent requirements that differentiate this industry from others, ensuring product reliability and performance.","status":"locked"},{"id":"UFM-003","title":"Overview of the IC Manufacturing Process","description":"This node provides a high-level overview of the intricate stages involved in manufacturing integrated circuits, showcasing the extreme display of technology and engineering. Students will learn about the seven key phases, from initial circuit design using EDA tools to final testing and packaging. We will explore how each step, including mask making, wafer manufacturing, thin film deposition, etching, ion implantation, and metal connection, contributes to transforming raw silicon into functional chips.","status":"locked"},{"id":"UFM-004","title":"Technological Pillars: Precision and Equipment","description":"Delve deeper into the technological intensity of advanced wafer manufacturing, focusing on the nano-level precision and specialized equipment. This node will highlight critical technologies like photolithography, chemical vapor deposition (CVD), and advanced etching machines, emphasizing their role in achieving sub-nanometer accuracy. Students will understand how these sophisticated tools are indispensable for creating complex circuit patterns and precisely modifying material properties to build functional ICs.","status":"locked"},{"id":"UFM-005","title":"Operational Excellence: Cleanrooms and Automation Systems","description":"Examine the paramount importance of ultra-clean environments and advanced automation in wafer fabrication. This node will detail the stringent cleanroom standards, far exceeding medical operating rooms, and the rigorous protocols for personnel entry to prevent any micro-contamination. Students will also learn about the sophisticated Automated Material Handling Systems (AMHS) and real-time dispatching systems (RTD) that minimize human intervention, maximize efficiency, and ensure high yield rates in production.","status":"locked"},{"id":"UFM-006","title":"Economic Landscape and Capital Intensity","description":"Understand the significant economic footprint and immense capital requirements of the advanced semiconductor manufacturing industry. This node will explain why 'Property, Plant, and Equipment' constitute a major asset on financial statements, driven by colossal capital expenditures for cutting-edge equipment like EUV lithography machines. Students will learn about the high costs associated with constructing and maintaining advanced fabs, along with the rapid equipment obsolescence due to continuous technological advancements.","status":"locked"}]}
