d the 'row by column' dot product rule and the specific conditions necessary for two matrices to be multiplied. We will explore important properties of matrix multiplication, including its non-commutative nature (AB ≠ BA), associativity ((AB)C = A(BC)), and distributivity (A(B+C) = AB + AC). Additionally, the concept of the identity matrix (I or Iₙ) will be introduced, highlighting its unique role as the multiplicative identity (AI = IA = A).","status":"locked"}]}
