NODE DESC: This node focuses on the transpose operation, denoted as Aᵀ. Students will learn how to obtain the transpose of a given matrix by interchanging its rows and columns. The lesson will also cover the key property that transposing a matrix twice returns the original matrix, i.e., (Aᵀ)ᵀ = A. Grasping the concept of transposition is essential for understanding various matrix properties, special matrix types, and advanced operations later on.
