NODE DESC: This node focuses on Gaussian elimination, the primary algorithm for systematically solving linear systems. We will detail the three elementary row operations: swapping two rows, multiplying a row by a non-zero scalar, and adding a multiple of one row to another. The main objective of Gaussian elimination is to transform the augmented matrix into row echelon form, where students will learn to identify pivots (the first non-zero element in each row) and understand the characteristic 'staircase' pattern of this form.
