NODE DESC: Upon achieving row echelon form, this node teaches how to interpret the resulting matrix to determine the nature of the linear system's solutions. Students will learn to distinguish between systems with a unique solution (when every variable corresponds to a pivot), no solution (indicated by a row like [0 0 ... 0 | b] where b ≠ 0), and infinite solutions. The concept of 'free variables,' which correspond to non-pivot columns and can take any value, will be explained as the source of infinite solutions, leading to parametric solution forms.
