Conducting System of the Heart  The heartbeat originates in a specialized cardiac muscle cells (cardiac conducting system) and spreads via this system to all parts of the myocardium.  Parts of conducting system:  1. Sinoatrial (SA) node is located in the posterior wall of right atrium (at the junction of the superior vena cava with the right atrium).  2. Atrioventricular (AV) node is located in the right posterior portion of interaterial septum  3. Bundle of His: located in the interventricular septum and divided into branches right and left.  4. Purkinje fibers: begin within the apex of the heart and extend through the walls of the ventricles.   This system has ability to stimulate cardiac contraction without any innervations.

